---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@/components/ui/Container.astro";
import Button from "@/components/ui/Button.astro";

const personSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Person",
  name: "Daniel Glazebrook",
  jobTitle: "Founder, Worm Studio",
  worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Worm Studio" },
  url: "https://wormstudio.co.uk/daniel-glazebrook",
  sameAs: "https://www.linkedin.com/in/daniel-james-glazebrook"
};
---

<Layout
  title="Daniel Glazebrook"
  description="About Worm Studio's founder, Daniel Glazebrook, and his background in SEO and web development."
  path="/daniel-glazebrook"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />

  <Container grid class="pt-20 pb-24">
    <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-8">
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted uppercase tracking-wide">Words from our founder</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold text-ink leading-tight mt-3">
        Worm Studio is a new agency, but its expertise isn't.
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="col-span-12 md:col-span-6 mt-8">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted">
        Worm Studio is new. I'm not - I've been working in SEO since 2012,
        and web development for longer than that. This studio is the first
        time I've put both under one name, not the first time I've done the
        work.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        I've watched search change more in the last two years than in the
        decade before it. Google went from ten blue links to AI Overviews.
        People stopped typing keywords into a search box and started asking
        ChatGPT a real question instead. Most of what I learned about
        ranking a page in 2012 still matters - structure, clarity, actually
        answering the question - but the destination changed, and a lot of
        agencies haven't caught up yet.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-gold pl-4 mt-6 text-ink font-display text-xl italic">
        "Worm Studio is my first independent studio, but it's not my first
        SEO project."
      </blockquote>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        I studied graphic design at the University of Brighton, then spent
        nine years as a full-stack web developer - mostly at small design
        agencies, the kind where there's no separate team for every job.
        You end up doing a bit of everything: design, build, content,
        client calls, and the SEO that made the site actually worth
        building in the first place. SEO was the constant through all of
        it - the part I kept coming back to, and the part I never stopped
        being genuinely into.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        That hands-on, involved-in-everything approach is the actual
        foundation <a href="/#approach" class="text-ink underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-gold-deep">Worm Studio's approach</a> is built on - not a pivot into something
        new, just the same way of working, applied to where search is now.
      </p>

      <p class="text-lg text-ink-muted mt-6">
        It's also why the first thing I did with this studio was check
        where it actually stood, in public, rather than just claim
        expertise - <a href="/blog/starting-from-zero-ai-search-baseline" class="text-ink underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-gold-deep">starting from zero</a> and documenting it honestly, results included.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <Button href="/#work" variant="outline">See how we work</Button>
        <Button href="/#approach" variant="text">Read our approach</Button>
        <Button href="/blog/starting-from-zero-ai-search-baseline" variant="text">Read the first case study</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>